            <div xml:id="d678">

                <pb facs="0739" n="635" sameAs="frus:frus1932v03/pg635"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">693.002 Manchuria/26: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Chargé in Great Britain (Atherton)</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-03-26T15:00:00-05:00">March 26, 1932—3 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>99. Department’s 88, March 11, 1 p.m. Your 111, March 16, 5 p.m., last sentence,
                    and your 107, March 12, noon.</p>
                <p>A. Under date March 22, 11 a.m., Minister Johnson telegraphs from Shanghai as follows:</p>
                <p>[Here follows quotation of telegram printed on <ref target="#pg616">page
                        616</ref>.]</p>
                <p>B. Under date March 26 [, 10 a.m.,] Minister Johnson telegraphs further from Shanghai as follows:</p>
                <p>[Here follows quotation of telegram printed on <ref target="#pg632">page
                        632</ref>.]</p>
                <p>C. Department feels that action such as suggested in its telegram under reference
                    is desirable and would be useful from point of view of future developments.</p>
                <p>D. Please report any developments by telegraph.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
